                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> Thanks for the fast response. This seems to add one extra whitespace to that first column which is fine. Next question is: is there a way to create \"recipes\" by binding all of that to one key after `ga` (e.g. override the behavior of `ga&`)?\r\n\r\nYes, there is. Through writing own modifier. That is, adding a function to `config.modifiers` following [this help entry](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-align.txt#L480). My previous suggestion translates like so:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.align').setup({\r\n  modifiers = {\r\n    ['&'] = function(steps, opts)\r\n      opts.split_pattern = '&'\r\n      table.insert(steps.pre_justify, MiniAlign.gen_step.trim())\r\n      opts.merge_delimiter = ' '\r\n    end\r\n  }\r\n})\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for the fast response. This seems to add one extra whitespace to that first column which is fine. Next question is: is there a way to create \"recipes\" by binding all of that to one key after <code class=\"notranslate\">ga</code> (e.g. override the behavior of <code class=\"notranslate\">ga&amp;</code>)?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, there is. Through writing own modifier. That is, adding a function to <code class=\"notranslate\">config.modifiers</code> following <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-align.txt#L480\">this help entry</a>. My previous suggestion translates like so:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"require('mini.align').setup({\n  modifiers = {\n    ['&amp;'] = function(steps, opts)\n      opts.split_pattern = '&amp;'\n      table.insert(steps.pre_justify, MiniAlign.gen_step.trim())\n      opts.merge_delimiter = ' '\n    end\n  }\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>mini.align<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">modifiers</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    [<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&amp;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>] <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">steps</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>)\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">split_pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&amp;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n      <span class=\"pl-c1\">table.insert</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">steps</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">pre_justify</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAlign</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_step</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">trim</span>())\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">merge_delimiter</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span> <span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n  }\n})</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Thanks for the fast response. This seems to add one extra whitespace to that first column which is fine. Next question is: is there a way to create \"recipes\" by binding all of that to one key after ga (e.g. override the behavior of ga&)?\n\nYes, there is. Through writing own modifier. That is, adding a function to config.modifiers following this help entry. My previous suggestion translates like so:\nrequire('mini.align').setup({\n  modifiers = {\n    ['&'] = function(steps, opts)\n      opts.split_pattern = '&'\n      table.insert(steps.pre_justify, MiniAlign.gen_step.trim())\n      opts.merge_delimiter = ' '\n    end\n  }\n})",
